        "original_id": "911bc535-cf41-52d0-a29d-186039299f1e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Xawery Żuławski, Brian G. Hutton, Sonia Bohosiewicz, Dorota Masłowska\n- Works: Polish-Russian War, Where Eagles Dare, Kelly's Heroes, Rezerwat, Obława, Czas honoru\n- Roles: film director, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Brian G. Hutton was born on January 1, 1935, and he was an American actor and film director.\n- Xawery Żuławski was born on 22 December 1971 in Warsaw, and he is a Polish film director.\n- Brian G. Hutton is most notably credited for directing the action films \"Where Eagles Dare\" (1968) and \"Kelly's Heroes\" (1970).\n- Polish-Russian War is a 2009 Polish film directed by Xawery Żuławski.\n- Polish-Russian War is based on the novel Polish-Russian War under the white-red flag by Dorota Masłowska.\n- Sonia Bohosiewicz appeared in the films \"Rezerwat,\" \"Obława,\" and \"Polish-Russian War,\" and in the television series \"Czas honoru.\"\n- Brian G. Hutton died on August 19, 2014.",
